  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe core idea is to use a hybrid optimization strategy combining a novel initialization based on sparse binary patterns and a two-stage optimization process. This approach addresses the non-convexity by leveraging binary patterns as a starting point for structured exploration, followed by a gradient-based refinement. The previous method's limitation of getting stuck in local minima is mitigated by using structured perturbations and a hybrid surrogated-exact objective regime. The binary initialization ensures balanced distribution of mass while allowing for flexible refinement through continuous parameters.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nRepresentation: Step function h: [0, 2] \u2192 [0, 1], discretized to n_points samples. \nVariables: \n- h_flat (n_points-length vector) with 0 \u2264 h_flat[i] \u2264 1\n- Target sum: target_sum = n_points / 2\n- dx = 2.0 / n_points\n\nObjective: Minimize C\u2085 = max_k \u222b h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx\nExact computation: np.correlate(h, 1 - h, mode=\"full\") * dx\nSurrogate: C\u2085_approx = (1/\u03b1) * ln(\u03a3 exp(\u03b1 * overlap_k)) for \u03b1=5000\n\nConstraints: \n- \u2211h_flat = target_sum\n- 0 \u2264 h_flat[i] \u2264 1\n\nOptimization:\n- SLSQP with bounds [0, 1] and equality constraint \u2211h_flat = target_sum\n- Post-optimization validation using exact evaluator\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nInitialize:\n- If initial_h_values is provided, use it as starting point\n- Else: Generate sparse binary pattern:\n  - Randomly select m = n_points // 2 positions\n  - Set h_flat[i] = 1 for these positions, 0 otherwise\n  - Scale to meet \u2211h_flat = target_sum\n\nOptimization Loop:\n- Stage 1 (Surrogate-based):\n   - Use log-sum-exp surrogate with \u03b1=5000\n   - Run SLSQP with maxiter=100\n   - Apply structured perturbations: swap 0/1 at random positions every 5 iterations\n- Stage 2 (Exact-based):\n   - Switch to exact objective evaluation\n   - Run L-BFGS-B with maxiter=50\n   - Add Gaussian noise (\u03c3=0.02) to h_flat every 10 iterations\n   - Clamp and rescale after perturbations\n\nCandidate Acceptance:\n- Track best solution (lowest C\u2085)\n- Validate \u2211h_flat \u2248 target_sum (tolerance 1e-6)\n- Ensure all h_flat[i] \u2208 [0,1]\n\nTermination:\n- Stop when time budget exhausted or no improvement in 10 iterations\n- Return best solution and its C\u2085 bound\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\nDefault configuration:\n- n_points=200\n- Stage 1: SLSQP with \u03b1=5000, 100 iterations, structured perturbations\n- Stage 2: L-BFGS-B with 50 iterations, noise scaling \u03c3=0.02\n- Perturbations: swap 0/1 swaps every 5 iterations, Gaussian noise every 10\n\nVariations:\n- Binary initialization denser/further spaced (m= n_points//4 to m= n_points//2)\n- Surrogate \u03b1 values: 1000, 5000, 10000\n- Solver mix: COBYLA + L-BFGS-B\n- Noise patterns: uniform, Gaussian, Cauchy\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nTime allocation:\n- Stage 1: ~200s (100 iterations with SLSQP)\n- Stage 2: ~150s (50 iterations with L-BFGS-B)\n- Perturbations: 100s\n- Final refinement: 150s\n\nRobustness:\n- For nan values: clamp to [0,1] and rescale\n- For constraint violation: project to feasible region by adjusting values\n- Fallback: use initial_h_values if all optimizations fail\n- Early exit: if no improvement for 10 iterations\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nFeasibility checks:\n- \u2211h_flat \u2248 target_sum (tolerance 1e-6)\n- All h_flat[i] \u2208 [0,1]\n- C\u2085 bound is finite and matches exact evaluator\n\nFinal validation:\n- Re-evaluate candidate with exact objective\n- Compare with current best\n- Return (h_values, c5_bound, n_points) with n_points=200",
